From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 20:25:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10467/11362] Take the split: 2 clean batches for efficiency, 3
 with the tool loop on

Operator decision. Batches 1-2 (r11l,lp85 / ls20,wa30) keep the loop OFF and give
four games of adapter-free efficiency on one consistent config. Batches 3-5
(sp80,su15 / tu93,cn04 / m0r0,sk48) run with CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_TOOL_LOOP=selfparse
so the tool-gap mechanism finally gets live rows -- it has sat at 7 empty rows
with its ledger never created, which cannot distinguish "no tool is ever wanted"
from "we have barely looked".

Handover is by a watcher polling for the ls20-wa30 result FILE, not a timer. The
eval writes only at the end of a batch, so the file appearing is the only
reliable completion signal; a timed kill would discard hours of finished work
exactly as exp6753's TemporaryDirectory did.

Recorded with it: the two halves must never be pooled. Different configuration,
different measurement -- the same discipline that keeps the native and selfparse
transport cells in separate run directories. Writing that down now, because the
temptation to sum ten games into one efficiency figure will be strongest when the
last batch lands and the earlier context is gone.

